Horizon bundles glyphs from Microsoft Fluent UI System Icons.

    https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-system-icons
    Licensed under the MIT License. Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.

The icon paths are embedded in public/index.html as an inline SVG symbol
sheet, generated by tools/build-icons.js from the @fluentui/svg-icons
package. Regenerating them is only necessary when changing the icon set;
a normal clone needs no build step.

The Horizon brand mark (public/brand/mark.svg, and the generated icons in
public/brand) is original work and is not part of the Microsoft icon set.
A small number of interface glyphs are also original, drawn directly in
tools/build-html.js.

Horizon is not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft. It talks to
Microsoft Foundry Local, which is separate software with its own licence
and privacy terms:

    https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/foundry-local/

Microsoft, Azure, Foundry and Foundry Local are trademarks of the Microsoft
group of companies. Horizon uses these names only to identify the software
it connects to.

No Microsoft product artwork is distributed with Horizon. Where the About
page shows the Foundry Local icon, that image is read at runtime from the
copy installed on the user's own machine (src/brand.js) and remains
Microsoft's property. If Foundry Local is not installed, Horizon falls back
to its own original glyph and no Microsoft artwork is shown.

Models downloaded through Foundry Local carry their own licences, shown
in the model catalogue under Settings.